Source material
---------------
The guidance in this project is an original synthesis and paraphrase of
Google's publicly available Android design guidance (developer.android.com),
Material Design guidance (m3.material.io), Android and Jetpack release notes,
and Google's developer blog posts. No Google text is reproduced at length;
names of guidelines, components, tokens, and API symbols are used as names.
Google's published pages remain the authoritative and evolving source of
truth:

    https://developer.android.com/design/ui
    https://m3.material.io

Much developer.android.com content is published by Google under CC BY 4.0 and
its code samples under Apache 2.0 (see https://developers.google.com/terms/site-policies).
Where this project adapts such material, it is paraphrased and attributed by
link at the point of use. Those licenses do not necessarily cover all Material
Design site content, imagery, or blog media, and nothing here relicenses
Google's content under MIT.

Factual statements (release dates, API levels, library versions, dimensions)
reflect Google's published pages on the dates recorded in the skill's claim
ledger and CHANGELOG.md, and may since have changed. Values marked "derived"
were worked out by the authors and are not published by Google.

Interpretation
--------------
The philosophy and psychology material is the authors' interpretation, not text
published by Google. It maps independently published design and cognitive
principles to the guidance they help explain, to make the guidance
understandable and generative.

